questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Spring Boot REST API experiences continuous Metaspace/Heap growth and eventual `OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space`. The service uses thread pooling for request handling. A code review reveals the following custom request filter:

java
@Component
public class RequestContextFilter implements Filter {
    private static final ThreadLocal<RequestContext> CONTEXT_HOLDER = 
        ThreadLocal.withInitial(RequestContext::new);

    @Override
    public void doFilter(ServletRequest req, ServletResponse res, FilterChain chain) 
            throws IOException, ServletException {
        RequestContext context = CONTEXT_HOLDER.get();
        context.setUserData(extractUserData(req));
        try {
            chain.doFilter(req, res);
        } finally {
            // Context reset logic omitted
        }
    }
}
